					Migadu speaks standard IMAP, so mailbox data moves cleanly with <code>imapsync</code>.
					Stand up Vectis Mail on a fresh VPS, recreate your domains and mailboxes, sync each
					mailbox over IMAP, publish new DKIM/SPF/DMARC records (Vectis generates the values),
					then cut your MX over once you've verified delivery. Plan a short cutover window during
					DNS propagation for small installs. Because the new IP starts cold, give it a warmup
					window before high outbound volume — see the <a href="/deliverability/">deliverability guide</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

